ram_pg.select_mode.explained.header=Modes explained:
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.fifo=§eFIFO§r - First In First Out:\nAfter having 2 portals active, each new portal will replace the oldest one.
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.lifo=§eLIFO§r - Last In First Out:\nAfter having 2 portals active, each new portal will replace the newest one.
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.multipair=§eMulti-Pair§r:\nAllows you to have multiple pairs of portals active at the same time (maximum of 10). You can enter any portal and come out from its pair.
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.root=§eRoot§r:\nShoots a portal that acts as an anchor. You can shoot multiple portals (maximum of 10), but when you enter one, you will always come out from the root portal (the first one created). Entering the root portal will take you back to the last portal you shooted.
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.custom=§eCUSTOM§r:\nAct exactly as Root mode, but the root portal is always in the custom location you've set. This mode is only active when you set a custom location.
ram_pg.select_mode.explained.target=§eTarget§r:\nSwing at the air, or crouch and jump, while aiming at a block to set it as the target. Your next portal links to a root portal opened exactly at that block (safe placement is ignored), and every portal after it works like Root mode. Setting a new target starts over.
ram_pg.target.marked=§aTarget set: X %s, Y %s, Z %s. Your next portal links to it.§r
ram_pg.target.none=§eNo target yet: swing at the air (or crouch and jump) while aiming at a block to set one.§r
ram_pg.target.no_block=§cNo block in sight to target.§r
ram_pg.select_mode.set_mode=§aSet Mode to %s.§r

